# Personal Task Manager — Core Rules

## Before coding
1. Read `AGENTS.md` and current phase in `docs/phases/phase-XX-*.md`
2. Stay within current phase scope unless user explicitly asks for more
3. Follow `docs/CONVENTIONS.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`

## Stack (do not change without user request)
- ASP.NET MVC 5 on .NET Framework 4.8
- EF6 Code First + Oracle
- Bootstrap 5, jQuery, Razor

## Security
- Never commit real connection strings or passwords
- Always filter data by current user (no cross-user access)
- Server-side validation required: `ModelState.IsValid`
- POST actions: `[ValidateAntiForgeryToken]`

## Git
- Branch: `feature/phase-XX-name` or `fix/description`
- Commit: `feat(scope): message` per CONVENTIONS.md
- Do not commit unless user asks

## Code quality
- ViewModels for views, not Entities
- Comment business logic in controllers/repositories
- Small focused diffs; match existing patterns
